<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kwan Phayao</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Phayao Lake</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kwan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phayao">Phayao</a> is a large freshwater lake beside the town of Phayao in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>. It is the largest freshwater lake of the north and an important fishery. The old city of Phayao, capital of a medieval Tai kingdom, stood on its shore, and the ruins of a temple, Wat Tilok Aram, lie submerged in the lake.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kwan-phayao.jpg" alt="Kwan Phayao" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chainwit. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunset_at_Kwan_Phayao_%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%A7%E0%B9%8A%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%B0%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2_(25-12-2021)_img_05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
